1
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:34,910
[In my prime]

2
00:01:35,310 --> 00:01:37,680
[Episode 7]

3
00:01:47,310 --> 00:01:48,440
Thank you, sweetie.

4
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:52,310
Dad.

5
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:55,210
The golden toads at Cao Xin's house

6
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,920
were all bought from you.

7
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,040
It's been over ten years.

8
00:02:00,070 --> 00:02:01,330
I'm very magnanimous.

9
00:02:02,310 --> 00:02:03,120
The past

10
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,040
is in the past.

11
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:05,640
Doesn't Uncle Cao

12
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:06,760
think the same way?

13
00:02:08,470 --> 00:02:09,000
But

14
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:09,960
then again...

15
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:12,240
Fortunately, I was laid off early,

16
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:14,430
and your mom had the foresight

17
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:16,680
to start this small business early

18
00:02:16,750 --> 00:02:17,800
and get a head start.

19
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,840
Look at the people being laid off now.

20
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:21,360
It's hard for them to take our place.

21
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,000
So,

22
00:02:22,430 --> 00:02:23,890
people should be content.

23
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:27,680
Dad.

24
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,490
When I get into Beining University

25
00:02:30,710 --> 00:02:32,240
and become a big boss after graduation,

26
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:33,300
you can work for me.

27
00:02:33,310 --> 00:02:35,120
I'll make sure you never get laid off.

28
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,720
You really are my sweet girl,

29
00:02:37,190 --> 00:02:38,680
so warm and caring.

30
00:02:39,190 --> 00:02:39,750
But,

31
00:02:40,750 --> 00:02:41,470
about Uncle Cao

32
00:02:41,470 --> 00:02:43,240
buying this golden toad,

33
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:44,520
you must not tell your mom.

34
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:45,120
Got it?

35
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:46,090
Don't worry.

36
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:48,240
Come sit up front.

37
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:48,800
Okay.

38
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:49,600
I will take you

39
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:52,079
for a ride in a convertible.

40
00:02:52,079 --> 00:02:52,630
Let's go!

41
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:53,240
Sit tight.

42
00:02:54,030 --> 00:02:55,000
Let's go!

43
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:57,960
Slow down.

44
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,520
You are really something.

45
00:03:13,150 --> 00:03:14,430
No wonder the pointer
on the electricity meter

46
00:03:14,430 --> 00:03:15,590
keeps spinning.

47
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,680
You have too much energy to burn,
don't you?

48
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:19,120
Fine,

49
00:03:19,630 --> 00:03:20,560
then get to work.

50
00:03:23,030 --> 00:03:24,190
If you don't finish
shelling these peanuts today,

51
00:03:24,190 --> 00:03:26,050
don't even think about sleeping.

52
00:03:52,630 --> 00:03:54,260
No matter how big the mistake is,

53
00:03:54,260 --> 00:03:55,590
you still have to let the kid eat.

54
00:03:55,590 --> 00:03:56,150
Shut up.

55
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:59,020
I'm disciplining the kid.

56
00:03:59,150 --> 00:04:00,360
Don't interrupt me.

57
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:02,010
It's always like this.

58
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:03,080
I pull on one side,

59
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:03,750
and you pull on the other.

60
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:05,750
Are you playing tug-of-war with me?

61
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:08,080
She doesn't sleep at night,

62
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,680
just sitting around
coming up with wicked ideas.

63
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:11,240
Doesn't she have energy to spare?

64
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,770
Then let her do some chores.

65
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:15,030
Doing chores is good.

66
00:04:15,710 --> 00:04:17,360
It's a good way to exercise.

67
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:19,500
Didn't the teacher say

68
00:04:19,870 --> 00:04:22,000
the college entrance exam
is not just about brainpower,

69
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,530
but also physical fitness?

70
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:24,860
Just eat your food.

71
00:04:25,750 --> 00:04:27,120
She's full of bad ideas.

72
00:04:28,430 --> 00:04:30,490
I don't know who this kid takes after.

73
00:04:41,190 --> 00:04:43,190
If you leave, I won't see you off.

74
00:04:43,830 --> 00:04:44,510
If you come,

75
00:04:45,159 --> 00:04:47,420
no matter how heavy the wind and rain are,

76
00:04:48,159 --> 00:04:49,290
I will go pick you up.

77
00:04:51,159 --> 00:04:52,420
Writing a love letter?

78
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,000
No.

79
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:53,920
Practicing handwriting.

80
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:54,870
Who are you trying to fool?

81
00:04:54,870 --> 00:04:56,440
Practicing handwriting on pink stationery?

82
00:04:56,440 --> 00:04:57,120
Come, let me see.

83
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:57,870
No.

84
00:04:57,890 --> 00:04:58,540
Let me see.

85
00:04:58,570 --> 00:04:59,150
No.

86
00:04:59,270 --> 00:04:59,930
Guys,

87
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,120
Qi Zhi wrote a love letter.

88
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:01,950
Come and see!

89
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:29,560
Xin,

90
00:05:29,750 --> 00:05:30,350
come here.

91
00:05:30,510 --> 00:05:30,830
Xin,

92
00:05:30,890 --> 00:05:32,510
take this chicken soup over
to the house across the street.

93
00:05:32,510 --> 00:05:33,800
Qi Zhi isn't home today.

94
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:34,360
No one will drink it.

95
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:36,270
Qi Zhi isn't here, but Qi Ni is.

96
00:05:36,790 --> 00:05:38,050
Grandpa, listen to me.

97
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:39,720
She and her mom are on the same side.

98
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:41,650
She won't drink your chicken soup.

99
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:43,170
I'm telling you,

100
00:05:43,310 --> 00:05:44,270
she will definitely drink it.

101
00:05:44,270 --> 00:05:44,680
Here,

102
00:05:45,390 --> 00:05:46,120
take it.

103
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:13,430
Damn Cao Xin.

104
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:15,850
At least you have a conscience.

105
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,170
Where did you go?

106
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:00,280
What was that noise outside?

107
00:07:00,950 --> 00:07:01,560
Was someone

108
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:02,600
rattling our iron gate?

109
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:03,160
No.

110
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:04,240
A cat.

111
00:07:04,870 --> 00:07:06,240
I don't know whose cat it was,

112
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:07,370
but I chased it away.

113
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:11,020
Are you really that obedient?

114
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:12,840
Our daughter hasn't eaten all night.

115
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:14,040
Didn't you even think

116
00:07:14,190 --> 00:07:15,510
about sneaking her some food?

117
00:07:15,510 --> 00:07:17,070
Honey, what are you talking about?

118
00:07:17,070 --> 00:07:18,300
Am I that kind of person?

119
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:19,660
I firmly follow

120
00:07:19,690 --> 00:07:21,220
and uphold your decisions.

121
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:23,040
You're right.

122
00:07:23,830 --> 00:07:26,230
This girl is too naughty
and needs a lesson.

123
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:26,750
I think

124
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:28,680
you did absolutely nothing wrong.

125
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,920
I thought you had some backbone.

126
00:07:33,310 --> 00:07:34,180
But when you were starving,

127
00:07:34,180 --> 00:07:35,980
you still drank my chicken soup.

128
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:38,700
It's called returning a favor.
Don't you get it?

129
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,960
That bunch of golden toads at your house

130
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,270
was bought from us too.

131
00:07:44,890 --> 00:07:45,750
I was wondering where

132
00:07:45,750 --> 00:07:46,500
those ugly toads

133
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:47,270
came from.

134
00:07:47,630 --> 00:07:48,270
Turns out

135
00:07:48,270 --> 00:07:49,920
they crawled in from your house.

136
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:51,310
I thought my dad's taste

137
00:07:51,330 --> 00:07:52,920
wouldn't be so bad as to buy that.

138
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:54,240
So he was secretly

139
00:07:54,390 --> 00:07:55,920
supporting your business.

140
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:56,720
Stop.

141
00:07:57,510 --> 00:07:59,159
You don't have to be so mean.

142
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:02,040
No one forced your family to buy them.

143
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,120
Your dad did it willingly.

144
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:03,920
Then are you drinking this chicken soup

145
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:05,120
of your own free will?

146
00:08:07,830 --> 00:08:09,030
Don't let my mom know.

147
00:08:09,070 --> 00:08:10,470
You mean buying the toads

148
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:12,380
or drinking the chicken soup?

149
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:15,720
Figure it out yourself.

150
00:08:16,230 --> 00:08:16,760
Hurry up.

151
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:18,600
Stop rushing me.

152
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:31,390
Dad.

153
00:08:31,630 --> 00:08:32,360
Drink it all?

154
00:08:33,270 --> 00:08:33,870
Yes.

155
00:08:35,909 --> 00:08:36,960
Come on, drink it quickly.

156
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:38,150
I just heated it up for you.

157
00:08:38,150 --> 00:08:38,909
Finish it.

158
00:08:39,030 --> 00:08:41,429
Then go do two sets of exercises
right away.

159
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:54,440
Dad.

160
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:55,550
Did you buy

161
00:08:55,550 --> 00:08:56,720
all these things from

162
00:08:56,720 --> 00:08:57,250
Uncle Qi?

163
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,720
Who told you that?

164
00:08:59,750 --> 00:09:00,870
Is that true?

165
00:09:02,150 --> 00:09:04,610
Your Uncle Qi's family
is having a hard time.

166
00:09:04,790 --> 00:09:06,650
It doesn't matter who we buy from.

167
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:08,550
Helping others is helping ourselves.

168
00:09:08,550 --> 00:09:09,750
We are all neighbors.

169
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:10,600
Right?

170
00:09:11,910 --> 00:09:12,440
Come.

171
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:13,620
About this,

172
00:09:14,510 --> 00:09:15,750
don't tell Mrs. Huo.

173
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:17,030
No.

174
00:09:17,030 --> 00:09:18,960
What exactly happened to Mrs. Huo?

175
00:09:19,150 --> 00:09:21,150
Why is everyone keeping it a secret?

176
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,120
Class 1, come in.

177
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:28,670
Talent.

178
00:09:29,030 --> 00:09:29,750
That's talent.

179
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:30,840
Quiet down, everyone.

180
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,440
I have something to tell you.

181
00:09:33,140 --> 00:09:33,840
The school sports meet

182
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:34,840
is about to start.

183
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:35,440
I know everyone

184
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:37,240
has been
under a lot of study pressure lately.

185
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:38,300
But the sports meet

186
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:40,080
is not just a test

187
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:41,240
of individual ability;

188
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:42,980
it also represents class honor.

189
00:09:42,980 --> 00:09:44,180
So I hope everyone can

190
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:45,530
participate actively.

191
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:47,000
Those who placed last year,

192
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:47,690
I've already

193
00:09:47,690 --> 00:09:48,570
signed you up.

194
00:09:48,950 --> 00:09:50,000
This year, we must

195
00:09:50,030 --> 00:09:51,610
win first place as a team.

196
00:09:52,030 --> 00:09:53,890
We can't let Class 2 take it again.

197
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:55,030
Monitor.

198
00:09:55,670 --> 00:09:56,560
Does that mean

199
00:09:56,580 --> 00:09:58,570
we don't have to sign up
if we have no special skills?

200
00:09:58,570 --> 00:09:59,170
All events

201
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,600
must have participants.

202
00:10:00,630 --> 00:10:01,290
How about this?

203
00:10:01,290 --> 00:10:02,440
If any event needs someone,

204
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:03,240
you'll fill in.

205
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:04,040
Stop messing around.

206
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:04,670
With my small build,

207
00:10:04,670 --> 00:10:05,530
don't you know?

208
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:06,640
I'd better just

209
00:10:06,670 --> 00:10:07,600
be a cheerleader

210
00:10:07,750 --> 00:10:09,510
and cheer for our classmates.

211
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:10,960
Go! Go! Go!

212
00:10:14,790 --> 00:10:15,930
Why can't you compete?

213
00:10:15,930 --> 00:10:16,930
If it were a long-face competition,

214
00:10:16,930 --> 00:10:19,150
you'd definitely come first in the grade.

215
00:10:19,150 --> 00:10:20,360
You talk too much.

216
00:10:23,030 --> 00:10:24,550
Shot put or medicine ball?

217
00:10:29,990 --> 00:10:32,030
[Qi Shi]

218
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:39,290
What's going on?

219
00:10:40,030 --> 00:10:41,580
For the women's 4x200 relay,

220
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:43,510
why is Qi Shi the only one signed up?

221
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,160
No one wants to run with Qi Shi.

222
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:46,000
They say it's a waste of time.

223
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,730
We'll definitely lose anyway.

224
00:10:48,670 --> 00:10:49,930
Then what should we do?

225
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:51,480
Our class doesn't have enough people.

226
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:52,540
We have to forfeit.

227
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,550
Why don't you go talk to Qi Shi

228
00:10:54,550 --> 00:10:55,810
and tell her not to run?

229
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:56,750
With her physical condition,

230
00:10:56,750 --> 00:10:57,390
there's no point in running.

231
00:10:57,390 --> 00:10:59,720
It would only cause trouble for our class.

232
00:11:02,270 --> 00:11:03,200
I'll go find her.

233
00:11:03,670 --> 00:11:05,240
Are you playing soccer later?

234
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:08,550
[Qing Wu First Senior High School]

235
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:14,580
Here's the situation.

236
00:11:16,070 --> 00:11:16,840
I asked

237
00:11:16,870 --> 00:11:18,130
the other classmates.

238
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:19,550
Everyone thinks

239
00:11:20,650 --> 00:11:21,720
your physical condition

240
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:23,480
might not be suitable for the competition.

241
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:24,200
Look,

242
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,620
for the 4x200m relay,

243
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:28,790
if you sign up alone,

244
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:30,650
you can't participate.

245
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:31,840
How about...

246
00:11:33,550 --> 00:11:34,270
Cao Xin,

247
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:36,440
tell me,

248
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,600
do you ever feel

249
00:11:40,750 --> 00:11:42,720
like there can only be one winner?

250
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:48,150
Setting aside our families' relationship,

251
00:11:48,150 --> 00:11:49,360
I admit you're excellent

252
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:50,560
and have good grades.

253
00:11:51,030 --> 00:11:52,560
But when it comes to grades,

254
00:11:53,150 --> 00:11:54,120
either you come first

255
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:55,080
or I do.

256
00:11:55,390 --> 00:11:57,000
We're neck and neck.

257
00:11:57,790 --> 00:11:59,120
As for handling things,

258
00:11:59,870 --> 00:12:01,730
you're steady, and I'm flexible.

259
00:12:01,850 --> 00:12:03,240
But every year
for the class monitor election,

260
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:04,370
I never get elected.

261
00:12:05,630 --> 00:12:07,360
Where do you think I fall short?

262
00:12:11,150 --> 00:12:12,280
Don't overthink it.

263
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:15,000
They're just talking nonsense.

264
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:20,200
Since I was little,
they called me "White-Haired Girl"

265
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,510
and called me a monster.

266
00:12:21,510 --> 00:12:22,770
I refused to accept it,

267
00:12:22,910 --> 00:12:24,080
so I fought them.

268
00:12:25,060 --> 00:12:25,840
After that,

269
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:27,800
they didn't dare bully me anymore.

270
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:29,480
I thought

271
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:32,330
I'd become like everyone else.

272
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:36,510
But I hadn't.

273
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:40,160
I hadn't become like everyone else.

274
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:42,260
But later on,

275
00:12:43,510 --> 00:12:44,390
everyone began to

276
00:12:44,390 --> 00:12:45,390
overprotect me

277
00:12:45,670 --> 00:12:47,470
and show me excessive sympathy.

278
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:49,450
During group cleanups,

279
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:51,140
they gave me the easiest jobs.

280
00:12:51,150 --> 00:12:52,750
They wouldn't let me take PE.

281
00:12:53,550 --> 00:12:54,200
I know

282
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:56,080
they mean well.

283
00:12:57,510 --> 00:12:58,630
But the more they

284
00:12:58,670 --> 00:12:59,670
tiptoed around me

285
00:12:59,670 --> 00:13:02,800
and avoided mentioning my illnes
for fear of hurting me,

286
00:13:04,390 --> 00:13:05,270
the more I felt

287
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:09,120
that it was just another way

288
00:13:09,790 --> 00:13:11,000
of reminding me

289
00:13:12,670 --> 00:13:14,930
that I was different from everyone else.

290
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:18,580
Running for class monitor

291
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:21,360
and joining the sports meet,

292
00:13:22,630 --> 00:13:24,320
I only wanted to prove

293
00:13:25,030 --> 00:13:26,960
that I was just like everyone else.

294
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:29,120
I'm not a sore loser.

295
00:13:29,670 --> 00:13:30,630
I don't care

296
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:31,790
whether I was elected

297
00:13:31,790 --> 00:13:32,550
or whether anyone

298
00:13:32,550 --> 00:13:33,790
wanted to run with me.

299
00:13:37,910 --> 00:13:39,630
I just wanted a chance,

300
00:13:42,240 --> 00:13:44,440
a fair chance to compete.

301
00:13:47,670 --> 00:13:48,470
Even if I lost,

302
00:13:48,630 --> 00:13:50,910
I wanted to lose fair and square.

303
00:14:05,270 --> 00:14:05,870
Cao,

304
00:14:06,750 --> 00:14:07,720
come down and play football.

305
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:09,720
Hurry up. The game is about to start.

306
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,120
What a shame.

307
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:23,250
I don't mean you.

308
00:14:23,390 --> 00:14:24,240
I mean Qi Shi.

309
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:26,480
Even though she's so competitive,

310
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:28,080
she's actually had it tough.

311
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:30,080
Don't be mad at me for saying this.

312
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:31,880
If Qi Shi were the class monitor,

313
00:14:32,110 --> 00:14:33,840
she might not be worse than you.

314
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:39,960
No matter how capable she is

315
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,550
or how many first places she gets,

316
00:14:41,550 --> 00:14:43,000
the teachers always say,

317
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:45,170
"It's a pity she has this illness."

318
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:46,600
Speech contests,

319
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:47,440
pep rallies,

320
00:14:48,020 --> 00:14:48,840
all the chances to stand out

321
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:50,480
have been handed to you, haven't they?

322
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:51,800
Take yourself, for example.

323
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:52,790
You two are neighbors

324
00:14:52,790 --> 00:14:53,990
who grew up together.

325
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:55,450
Whenever she beats you,

326
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:56,850
haven't you thought

327
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:58,620
that, in the competition between you two,

328
00:14:58,620 --> 00:15:00,350
she's always just an outsider?

329
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:01,100
No matter how capable she is,

330
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:03,160
she's never really taken seriously.

331
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:16,480
Tianji!

332
00:15:17,030 --> 00:15:17,690
Over there!

333
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:20,320
Nice shot!

334
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:20,890
Over there!

335
00:15:20,890 --> 00:15:22,090
Nice shot! Nice shot!

336
00:15:44,390 --> 00:15:45,120
Go play goalie!

337
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:45,520
Shoot!

338
00:15:47,390 --> 00:15:47,910
Attack!

339
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:55,690
Are you okay?

340
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:56,820
Cao Xin,

341
00:15:57,030 --> 00:15:58,230
can you keep playing?

342
00:15:58,910 --> 00:16:00,410
Do you want to rest for a while?

343
00:16:00,410 --> 00:16:01,000
No, no.

344
00:16:01,510 --> 00:16:02,000
Come on.

345
00:16:03,850 --> 00:16:05,380
Are you sure you can do this?

346
00:16:22,270 --> 00:16:22,550
Zhi.

347
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:25,270
Did you run all the way back

348
00:16:25,270 --> 00:16:26,320
from the provincial sports school again?

349
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:27,720
How did you know it was me?

350
00:16:27,870 --> 00:16:28,720
I could smell your sweat

351
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:29,910
from far away.

352
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:31,360
I brought you chocolate,

353
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:33,120
and you still complain about me.

354
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:34,320
My bad, my bad, my bad.

355
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:37,870
Zhi,

356
00:16:38,150 --> 00:16:40,010
can I discuss something with you?

357
00:16:40,100 --> 00:16:41,560
Can you teach me how to run?

358
00:16:43,390 --> 00:16:44,740
Why would you want to
run with your condition?

359
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:45,510
If Mom finds out,

360
00:16:45,510 --> 00:16:46,840
she'll scold me to death.

361
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:47,550
Whatever.

362
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:49,850
Forget it if you won't teach me.

363
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:50,870
No.

364
00:16:50,870 --> 00:16:52,030
Why are you so impulsive?

365
00:16:52,030 --> 00:16:53,230
Pick something else.

366
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,100
Let's talk about it. Pick something else.

367
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:56,100
Anything is fine.

368
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:57,800
Pass it quickly. Over there!

369
00:16:59,870 --> 00:17:00,670
Time's up!

370
00:17:03,270 --> 00:17:04,270
That wasn't easy.

371
00:17:04,750 --> 00:17:05,609
I'm exhausted.

372
00:17:06,109 --> 00:17:07,510
I didn't expect us to tie.

373
00:17:07,550 --> 00:17:09,530
We went easy on you. Couldn't you tell?

374
00:17:09,530 --> 00:17:10,859
Your goalie is injured.

375
00:17:11,510 --> 00:17:12,810
We just didn't feel like playing you.

376
00:17:12,810 --> 00:17:14,069
A tie is a tie.

377
00:17:14,069 --> 00:17:15,069
Stop pretending.

378
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:18,560
Who are you saying is pretending?

379
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:19,240
You really don't know
what's good for you, do you?

380
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:20,300
I'm saying you are.

381
00:17:20,349 --> 00:17:21,240
Who are you talking about?

382
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:22,270
Who are you talking about?

383
00:17:22,270 --> 00:17:22,480
Enough, enough.

384
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:23,069
I'm saying you are.

385
00:17:23,069 --> 00:17:23,720
Who are you saying is pretending?

386
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:28,270
Enough, enough, enough.

387
00:17:33,310 --> 00:17:34,310
Is your foot okay?

388
00:17:34,550 --> 00:17:36,080
Let me push the bike for you.

389
00:17:40,270 --> 00:17:42,530
I'm thinking about what Qi Shi just said.

390
00:17:44,510 --> 00:17:45,510
For so many years,

391
00:17:46,240 --> 00:17:47,500
I've never beaten her.

392
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:50,000
The only thing I have over her

393
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,240
is

394
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:52,720
being an ordinary person.

395
00:17:53,270 --> 00:17:54,930
Why are you being so profound?

396
00:17:54,950 --> 00:17:56,080
I don't quite get it.

397
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:57,000
I think

398
00:17:57,090 --> 00:17:58,310
you're just under too much pressure.

399
00:17:58,310 --> 00:17:58,920
How about

400
00:17:59,270 --> 00:18:00,680
I take you somewhere to relax

401
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:02,010
and blow off some steam?

402
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:02,960
Want to go to an

403
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:03,820
Internet cafe?

404
00:18:06,130 --> 00:18:08,280
You can choose from
all kinds of online games.

405
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:09,570
That latest game,

406
00:18:09,750 --> 00:18:10,950
I'm really good at it.

407
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:13,960
I'm not afraid of
playing one-on-one or in a group.

408
00:18:14,270 --> 00:18:15,870
Do more practice questions.

409
00:18:16,310 --> 00:18:19,640
Otherwise, your mom will beat you again
after the next exam.

410
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:22,560
Cao Xin, you're back.

411
00:18:36,350 --> 00:18:37,400
What do you want to do?

412
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:38,640
Are you trying to snitch on me?

413
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:40,570
Some other time. My mom's not home.

414
00:18:44,310 --> 00:18:44,830
Qi Shi.

415
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:49,340
Let's compete fairly, just once.

416
00:18:57,790 --> 00:18:59,830
You're not staying home on the weekend?

417
00:18:59,830 --> 00:19:00,960
Where are you going?

418
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,480
I'm... going to school.

419
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:04,160
To school?

420
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:05,790
Mrs. Huo.

421
00:19:07,920 --> 00:19:08,450
Let's go.

422
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:11,830
Go ahead.

423
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:13,240
Come back early.

424
00:19:14,310 --> 00:19:15,570
I'm leaving, Mrs. Huo.

425
00:19:19,750 --> 00:19:21,270
Where are you going?

426
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:23,350
Can't any of you stay at home?

427
00:19:23,350 --> 00:19:23,940
It's the weekend,

428
00:19:23,940 --> 00:19:25,470
and you're all running out.

429
00:19:26,070 --> 00:19:26,680
You're going out

430
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:28,110
in white sneakers?

431
00:19:28,270 --> 00:19:29,000
If you go out,

432
00:19:29,020 --> 00:19:30,150
they'll get ruined.

433
00:19:30,270 --> 00:19:31,000
Wash them yourself

434
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:31,880
when you get back.

435
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:32,640
I'll wash them myself, Mom.

436
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:33,970
I'm going out for a walk.

437
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:35,590
Get back in the house.

438
00:19:35,590 --> 00:19:37,050
Don't idle around all day.

439
00:19:37,330 --> 00:19:38,030
Wash all the clothes

440
00:19:38,030 --> 00:19:38,720
you brought back

441
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:39,350
yourself.

442
00:19:40,350 --> 00:19:42,010
I'll wash them when I get back.

443
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:43,600
Dad, I'm heading out.

444
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:48,220
Close the door.

445
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:02,750
Is walking around in broad daylight

446
00:20:02,750 --> 00:20:04,480
your idea of fair competition?

447
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:06,070
What if I say yes?

448
00:20:07,820 --> 00:20:09,620
Do you dare to listen to me today?

449
00:20:11,050 --> 00:20:12,210
Of course I dare.

450
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:13,310
Have I ever been afraid of you?

451
00:20:13,310 --> 00:20:13,910
All right.

452
00:20:14,750 --> 00:20:15,510
Aren't you going to participate

453
00:20:15,510 --> 00:20:16,840
in the sports meet race?

454
00:20:17,270 --> 00:20:18,130
I'll teach you.

455
00:20:18,750 --> 00:20:20,010
I've thought about it.

456
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:21,680
Your eyesight isn't very good,

457
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:23,270
but running is like doing math problems.

458
00:20:23,270 --> 00:20:24,670
Practice makes perfect.

459
00:20:24,750 --> 00:20:26,150
The track is only so wide.

460
00:20:26,830 --> 00:20:27,480
If you run enough,

461
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:29,310
your feet will naturally know the way.

462
00:20:29,310 --> 00:20:30,880
To be absolutely safe,

463
00:20:31,220 --> 00:20:32,200
I'll be on the sidelines

464
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:33,260
calling your name.

465
00:20:33,550 --> 00:20:34,360
Run toward

466
00:20:34,380 --> 00:20:35,460
my voice.

467
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:36,740
You'll be fine.

468
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:39,260
But this is a relay race after all.

469
00:20:39,480 --> 00:20:40,000
If we don't have enough people,

470
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,330
we still can't compete.

471
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:46,610
Bring her one week of free lunches.

472
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:49,030
Do her classroom-cleaning duty for a week.

473
00:20:49,030 --> 00:20:49,640
And

474
00:20:49,790 --> 00:20:51,270
do a week's worth of math homework for her.

475
00:20:51,270 --> 00:20:53,330
I've really pulled out all the stops.

476
00:20:55,030 --> 00:20:55,640
Thanks.

477
00:20:57,550 --> 00:20:59,200
Are you satisfied with

478
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:01,660
my organizational skills as class monitor?

479
00:21:02,440 --> 00:21:03,370
Very satisfied.

480
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:05,540
That's why you're the class monitor.

481
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:06,750
Let's go.

482
00:21:06,750 --> 00:21:08,080
I'll show you the track.

483
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:19,400
Isn't this just messing around?

484
00:21:19,400 --> 00:21:20,200
With Qi Shi's condition,

485
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:21,860
how can she train for running?

486
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:22,760
What's wrong?

487
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:25,830
I think compared to superficial injuries,

488
00:21:25,830 --> 00:21:28,360
making her happy
is the most important thing.

489
00:21:28,510 --> 00:21:29,200
Makes sense.

490
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:29,720
Right?

491
00:21:32,150 --> 00:21:32,970
What's Cao Xin

492
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,200
teaching her?

493
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:35,510
Qi Shi's running posture

494
00:21:35,510 --> 00:21:36,440
looks terrible.

495
00:21:37,070 --> 00:21:38,240
Who are you saying is a bad teacher?

496
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:39,900
He's teaching her quite well.

497
00:21:40,030 --> 00:21:40,400
No.

498
00:21:40,690 --> 00:21:41,880
If she's going to train,

499
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:42,350
she needs to do it properly.

500
00:21:42,350 --> 00:21:43,680
Otherwise, she could get hurt more easily.

501
00:21:43,680 --> 00:21:45,480
Isn't she practicing properly?

502
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:47,720
Let's go.

503
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:51,750
Qi Shi!

504
00:21:52,510 --> 00:21:53,000
Zhi.

505
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:54,210
Why are you here?

506
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:56,060
I asked Qi Zhi to come and help.

507
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:57,450
I have to say.

508
00:21:57,830 --> 00:21:58,350
You have a

509
00:21:58,350 --> 00:21:59,640
future Olympic champion right here,

510
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:00,960
but you asked an amateur to teach you.

511
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:02,240
Isn't that a waste of talent?

512
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:03,170
You refused

513
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:04,260
to teach me before.

514
00:22:04,510 --> 00:22:04,960
Qi Shi,

515
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:06,440
I brought you sunscreen.

516
00:22:06,440 --> 00:22:08,440
You can use it when the sun is strong.

517
00:22:09,080 --> 00:22:09,880
Maybe it'll be cloudy that day,

518
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:11,080
and you won't need it.

519
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:17,510
What's wrong, Zhi?

520
00:22:17,510 --> 00:22:18,070
Nothing.

521
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:19,960
Even if it's cloudy,

522
00:22:20,270 --> 00:22:22,030
UV rays are still strong,
so you need sunscreen,

523
00:22:22,030 --> 00:22:22,550
right?

524
00:22:23,650 --> 00:22:24,350
And hats and stuff,

525
00:22:24,350 --> 00:22:25,680
make sure you wear them.

526
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:26,820
But seriously,

527
00:22:26,830 --> 00:22:28,440
I'm worried about your health.

528
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:29,450
If it gets to be too much,

529
00:22:29,450 --> 00:22:30,440
tell me right away.

530
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:31,640
Don't push yourself.

531
00:22:33,830 --> 00:22:34,880
Maybe you should sit this one out.

532
00:22:34,880 --> 00:22:35,440
Zhi,

533
00:22:36,110 --> 00:22:37,640
I haven't even started yet.

534
00:22:38,270 --> 00:22:40,470
Come on, look at me. Lift your right leg.

535
00:22:40,810 --> 00:22:42,160
Hold this leg with both hands,

536
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:44,240
and bring your thigh as close
to your chest as possible.

537
00:22:44,240 --> 00:22:46,030
At the same time, relax this foot.

538
00:22:46,030 --> 00:22:46,920
Step forward.

539
00:22:47,830 --> 00:22:48,280
Right.

540
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:49,750
Pay attention to this foot.

541
00:22:49,750 --> 00:22:50,920
Don't flex or point it.

542
00:22:50,920 --> 00:22:51,920
You must relax it.

543
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:52,640
Okay?

544
00:22:52,790 --> 00:22:53,250
Come on.

545
00:22:53,740 --> 00:22:54,600
Come on, relax.

546
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,790
Right, hold it. Stand firm.

547
00:22:55,790 --> 00:22:57,160
Relax this foot. Don't tense up.

548
00:22:57,160 --> 00:22:57,960
Relax. Relax.

549
00:22:58,070 --> 00:22:59,270
Right, step forward.

550
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:00,400
Okay.

551
00:23:00,510 --> 00:23:00,920
Good.

552
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:03,720
That's enough.

553
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:04,440
Don't be too perfect,

554
00:23:04,440 --> 00:23:06,100
or my sister will get jealous.

555
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:09,920
Relax.

556
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:11,640
Make sure the foot underneath
stays relaxed.

557
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:12,030
Okay?

558
00:23:15,440 --> 00:23:16,920
Now, pay attention to this movement.

559
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:18,270
Don't let your knees go past your toes.

560
00:23:18,270 --> 00:23:20,530
Try to keep your weight on the right side.

561
00:23:20,590 --> 00:23:21,920
Then shift from this side

562
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:23,200
to the other side.

563
00:23:23,920 --> 00:23:25,350
Then face forward.

564
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:26,760
Face forward.

565
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:28,030
Right, turn to the front.

566
00:23:28,030 --> 00:23:28,940
You need to do both sides.

567
00:23:28,940 --> 00:23:29,590
Both sides are fine.

568
00:23:29,590 --> 00:23:30,340
Turn to the front.

569
00:23:30,340 --> 00:23:32,310
You two need to
swing your inner arms in sync.

570
00:23:32,310 --> 00:23:33,310
The rhythm must be exactly the same.

571
00:23:33,310 --> 00:23:35,000
Because you are going to
be her guide runner.

572
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:36,480
Your rope is a guide rope,

573
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:37,760
what keeps you together.

574
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:38,520
At the start,

575
00:23:38,550 --> 00:23:39,920
hold hands first

576
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:41,190
so you can find

577
00:23:41,190 --> 00:23:42,390
a shared rhythm.

578
00:23:42,480 --> 00:23:43,680
Right, move with your bodies.

579
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:44,880
Find a shared rhythm.

580
00:23:46,920 --> 00:23:48,520
Come, give me your left hand.

581
00:23:49,160 --> 00:23:50,490
Right, your right hand.

582
00:23:52,720 --> 00:23:53,920
Adjust it

583
00:23:53,920 --> 00:23:56,720
to a length
